/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A mixed section has one or more closed cells and at least one open wall ending in a free edge.
   - xS is the distance of the load line from the moment point O (mm); AR is the area enclosed by cell R (mm²); the moment of a constant cell flow about any point is 2AR qs,0,R, anticlockwise positive.
   - the rate of twist (rad/mm), from cell R only; the open walls do not appear because they enclose no area.
   - The open walls do twist with the section; they just add almost nothing to the torsional stiffness, since their torsion constant is Σbt³/3 against the 4A²/∮ds/t of the cell.
   - If the load line is known, the moment equation gives the constant directly and the twist equation gives the rate of twist.
*/
