/* book Worked example: Q: A wing section is idealised into six booms. The closed cell has booms 1 (0, 50), 2 (200, 50), 3 (200, −50) and 4 (0, −50) mm with areas 600, 800, 800 and 600 mm²; its spar webs are 2 mm and its skins 1.5 mm thick. Two open trailing panels run from booms 2 and 3 to booms 5 (300, 25) and 6 (300, −25), each 200 mm², which are free edges. A shear Sy = 10 kN acts along the front spar (x = 0). With G = 27 GPa, find the shear flows, the rate of twist and the shear centre.
   1. Ixx = 2 × (600 × 50² + 800 × 50² + 200 × 25²) = 7,250,000 mm⁴; Sy/Ixx = 1.3793 × 10⁻³ N/mm³.
   2. Open panels, from the free booms: q₅₂ = −0.001379 × 200 × 25 = −6.90 N/mm (from 5 to 2); q₆₃ = +6.90 N/mm (from 6 to 3).
   3. Cut the top skin 2–1. From boom 1 down the front spar: q₁₄ = −0.001379 × 600 × 50 = −41.38 N/mm. Boom 4 (y = −50) cancels it: q₄₃ = 0.
   4. Boom 3 receives q₆₃ and adds −k × 800 × (−50): q₃₂ = 0 + 6.90 + 55.17 = 62.07 N/mm up the rear spar. At boom 2, 62.07 + (−6.90) − 55.17 = 0, which matches the cut.
   5. Check: vertical forces 4,138 (front) + 6,207 (rear) − 2 × 172.4 (trailing panels) = 10,000 N = Sy.
   6. Moments about O, the front spar mid-point, anticlockwise positive: rear spar 200 × 6,207 = 1,241,379; each trailing panel −68,966; total 1,103,448 N·mm. The load passes through O, so 0 = 1,103,448 + 2 × 20,000 qs,0 and qs,0 = −27.59 N/mm.
   7. Final cell flows: front spar −68.97 (that is 68.97 upwards), bottom skin −27.59, rear spar 34.48, top skin −27.59 N/mm; trailing panels ±6.90 N/mm.
   8. Twist: ∮q ds/t = −9,080 N/mm, so dθ/dz = −9,080/(2 × 20,000 × 27,000) = −8.41 × 10⁻⁶ rad/mm = −0.482°/m, that is 0.482°/m clockwise (nose up for lift on the front spar).
   9. Shear centre: zero twist gives qs,0 = −∮qb ds/t ÷ ∮ds/t = −1,034.5/366.67 = −2.821 N/mm, and xS = (1,103,448 + 40,000 × −2.821)/10,000 = 99.1 mm behind the front spar.
   Answer: qs,0 = −27.59 N/mm; front spar 68.97 N/mm, rear spar 34.48 N/mm, skins 27.59 N/mm, trailing panels 6.90 N/mm; rate of twist 0.482° per metre, nose up; shear centre 99.1 mm behind the front spar. */
